 "result": "maze.py is a level-by-level BFS on a padded flat grid. A '#' border removes bounds checks, a bytearray marks visited cells, and no distance array is kept. It returns as soon as E is discovered, and returns -1 when there is no path or S/E is missing. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78). The variant was adopted on a +29% win (median 3.574 vs 2.763 for the prior body). Further tuning seems unlikely to beat the 3% margin enough to justify the cost, so I am stopping here.",
